[{"page": 1, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q5-1", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "T5. Cardiolipins", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 150.9783477783203, 179.86404418945312, 172.68597412109375]}, {"text": "6%", "bbox": [290.6499938964844, 193.6215057373047, 304.6280822753906, 207.18873596191406]}, {"text": "5.1", "bbox": [188.49600219726562, 209.5625, 202.5609893798828, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "5.2", "bbox": [220.1219940185547, 209.5625, 234.18698120117188, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "5.3", "bbox": [251.7480010986328, 209.5625, 265.8129577636719, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "5.4", "bbox": [283.3739929199219, 209.5625, 297.43896484375, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "5.5", "bbox": [315.0, 209.5625, 329.0649719238281, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "5.6", "bbox": [346.6260070800781, 209.5625, 360.69097900390625, 223.12973022460938]}, {"text": "Σ", "bbox": [389.4079895019531, 194.64697265625, 395.6246643066406, 229.23712158203125]}, {"text": "1", "bbox": [192.67999267578125, 225.50250244140625, 198.3763885498047, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "6", "bbox": [224.30599975585938, 225.50250244140625, 230.0023956298828, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "4", "bbox": [255.9320068359375, 225.50250244140625, 261.6283874511719, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [287.5579833984375, 225.50250244140625, 293.2543640136719, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "2", "bbox": [319.18402099609375, 225.50250244140625, 324.8804016113281, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "3", "bbox": [350.80999755859375, 225.50250244140625, 356.5063781738281, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "18", "bbox": [386.8190002441406, 225.50250244140625, 398.2139892578125, 239.06973266601562]}, {"text": "In this problem you are asked to be creative and build molecules from fragments. For instance, if you", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 259.33349609375, 538.5557861328125, 272.9007263183594]}, {"text": "are required to draw a chiral phospholipid such as W using fragments a-e, it can be assembled as shown", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 271.28851318359375, 538.5786743164062, 284.8557434082031]}, {"text": "below.", "bbox": [56.692962646484375, 283.2434997558594, 87.24891662597656, 296.81072998046875]}, {"text": "Cardiolipins are a family of acyclic phospholipids differing in fatty acid residues. They are essential for", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 457.3445129394531, 538.5650024414062, 470.9117431640625]}, {"text": "energy production and membrane stability. Defects can lead to certain diseases. PL1 belongs to this", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 469.3005065917969, 538.5733032226562, 482.86773681640625]}, {"text": "family. Using only the structural elements a-d in the quantities stated below, it is possible to assemble", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 481.2554931640625, 538.5802001953125, 494.8227233886719]}, {"text": "the non-ionised form of PL1. R is a hydrocarbon substituent in the fatty acid structure.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 493.2104797363281, 459.5451965332031, 506.7777099609375]}, {"text": "PL1 does not contain any peroxide bonds.", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 600.1644897460938, 252.990478515625, 613.731689453125]}, {"text": "5.1", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 623.1295166015625, 92.84233856201172, 636.6967163085938]}, {"text": "Tick one correct statement regarding the value of n (number of type a frag-", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 623.1295166015625, 480.5858154296875, 636.6967163085938]}, {"text": "ments).", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 635.0845336914062, 149.80982971191406, 648.6517333984375]}, {"text": "(a) n is an even number,", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 647.03955078125, 226.56520080566406, 660.6067504882812]}, {"text": "(b) n is an odd number,", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 658.9945678710938, 223.02951049804688, 672.561767578125]}, {"text": "(c) n can be either an odd or an even number.", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 670.9495849609375, 327.4753112792969, 684.5177612304688]}, {"text": "1.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 623.0535888671875, 521.8194580078125, 636.6207885742188]}, {"text": "Some cardiolipins are chiral molecules, even if they contain four identical fatty acid residues, as in the case", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 699.823486328125, 538.5836181640625, 713.3906860351562]}, {"text": "of PL1. One enantiomer of PL1 is found in prokaryotes and eukaryotes, and the other only in archaea. All", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 711.7785034179688, 538.5548095703125, 725.345703125]}, {"text": "other diastereomers of PL1 are achiral molecules, since they have a plane of symmetry. Do not consider", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 723.7344970703125, 538.5767822265625, 737.3016967773438]}, {"text": "the chirality of phosphorus atoms as stereocentres.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 735.6895141601562, 296.97161865234375, 749.2567138671875]}, {"text": "PL1 is a diprotic acid with the same acidic groups.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 753.6215209960938, 312.6356201171875, 767.188720703125]}, {"text": "Its second deprotonation is less favourable", "bbox": [324.11187744140625, 753.6215209960938, 538.576416015625, 767.188720703125]}, {"text": "(𝑝𝐾𝑎2 ≫𝑝𝐾𝑎1) due to the special, stable structure of monoanion Y.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 750.6619873046875, 370.16864013671875, 787.7431640625]}]}, {"page": 2, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q5-2", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "5.2", "bbox": [78.60800170898438, 166.2294921875, 92.84233856201172, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "Draw the structure of one enantiomer of PL1. Draw the structure of Y in a way", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 166.2294921875, 480.580078125, 179.79672241210938]}, {"text": "that shows the stabilisation that explains the difference between 𝑝𝐾𝑎1 and", "bbox": [114.69100952148438, 163.26898193359375, 461.4952697753906, 199.44757080078125]}, {"text": "𝑝𝐾𝑎2. Use the abbreviation R for the fatty acid residues.", "bbox": [114.6910400390625, 175.2249755859375, 373.289306640625, 211.40257263183594]}, {"text": "6.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 166.15451049804688, 521.8194580078125, 179.72174072265625]}, {"text": "A series of experiments was conducted to identify the fatty acid (RCOOH) in PL1 found predominantly", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 220.0185089111328, 538.5782470703125, 233.5857391357422]}, {"text": "in mammalian hearts. During reductive ozonolysis, RCOOH forms three different organic products in", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 231.9735107421875, 538.565673828125, 245.54074096679688]}, {"text": "equimolar amounts.", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 243.9285125732422, 151.64723205566406, 257.4957275390625]}, {"text": "5.3", "bbox": [78.60802459716797, 266.89349365234375, 92.84236145019531, 280.4607238769531]}, {"text": "Determine the molecular formula of the fatty acid (RCOOH), if the non-ionised", "bbox": [114.69256591796875, 266.89349365234375, 480.5820617675781, 280.4607238769531]}, {"text": "form of PL1 contains 255 𝜎and 𝜋bonds between atoms in total. Support your", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 263.9339599609375, 480.5856018066406, 298.52410888671875]}, {"text": "answer with calculations.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 293.09552001953125, 231.93154907226562, 306.6627502441406]}, {"text": "If you were unable to find the structural formula of PL1, you can use a-d fragments", "bbox": [114.69100189208984, 305.0505065917969, 480.57257080078125, 318.61773681640625]}, {"text": "from 5.1.", "bbox": [114.69097900390625, 317.0054931640625, 155.88462829589844, 330.5727233886719]}, {"text": "4.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 266.8184814453125, 521.8194580078125, 280.3857116699219]}, {"text": "100 g of RCOOH reacts with 181.0 g of iodine. RCOOH also reacts in similar way with X and forms an", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 346.6965026855469, 538.5682983398438, 360.26373291015625]}, {"text": "adduct with an iodine mass fraction of 36.57%.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 358.6514892578125, 274.635498046875, 372.2187194824219]}, {"text": "5.4", "bbox": [78.60799407958984, 381.6164855957031, 92.84233093261719, 395.1837158203125]}, {"text": "Determine the molecular formula of X. Support your answer with calculations.", "bbox": [114.69253540039062, 381.6164855957031, 480.5780334472656, 395.1837463378906]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 381.54150390625, 521.8194580078125, 395.1087341308594]}, {"text": "The phase behavior of PL1 depends on pH. In physiological conditions, PL1 is a dianion and it forms a", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 414.5954895019531, 538.567626953125, 428.1627197265625]}, {"text": "lamellar phase.", "bbox": [56.693023681640625, 426.55047607421875, 128.1454620361328, 440.1177062988281]}, {"text": "5.5", "bbox": [78.60802459716797, 449.5154724121094, 92.84236145019531, 463.08270263671875]}, {"text": "Which lipid phase is formed by PL1 when both acid residues in it are protonated?", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 449.5154724121094, 480.57696533203125, 463.08270263671875]}, {"text": "Note that knowledge of PL1 structure is not required to solve this question.", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 461.470458984375, 466.9203796386719, 475.0376892089844]}, {"text": "Tick the correct answer.", "bbox": [114.69102478027344, 473.4254455566406, 227.62091064453125, 486.99273681640625]}, {"text": "(a) micellar", "bbox": [141.16500854492188, 641.5905151367188, 192.443359375, 655.15771484375]}, {"text": "(b) lamellar", "bbox": [244.3179931640625, 641.5905151367188, 296.94134521484375, 655.15771484375]}, {"text": "(c) hexagonal", "bbox": [343.281005859375, 641.5905151367188, 405.6350402832031, 655.15771484375]}, {"text": "(d) inverse", "bbox": [453.9840087890625, 635.6124877929688, 502.58123779296875, 649.1796875]}, {"text": "hexagonal", "bbox": [453.7799987792969, 647.5675048828125, 502.7940979003906, 661.1347045898438]}, {"text": "2.0 pt", "bbox": [495.45001220703125, 449.43951416015625, 521.8194580078125, 463.0067443847656]}]}, {"page": 3, "width": 595.280029296875, "height": 841.8900146484375, "mode": "native", "lines": [{"text": "Theory", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 63.1240119934082, 105.85767364501953, 82.42530822753906]}, {"text": "Q5-3", "bbox": [410.3869934082031, 59.77293014526367, 538.61376953125, 136.97825622558594]}, {"text": "English (Official)", "bbox": [460.8269958496094, 128.718505859375, 535.9927978515625, 142.28573608398438]}, {"text": "The following balanced reaction equations show the hydrolysis of phospholipids PL1-PL3:", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 155.21949768066406, 474.5105895996094, 168.78672790527344]}, {"text": "- The non-ionised form of PL2 contains 254 𝜎and 𝜋bonds between atoms in total. It is a chiral and a", "bbox": [56.69300079345703, 308.5619812011719, 538.5755615234375, 343.1521301269531]}, {"text": "more symmetrical molecule than PL1,", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 335.4335021972656, 233.75363159179688, 349.000732421875]}, {"text": "- Z contains C, H, and O only, and it doesn’t react with H2 in the presence of a catalyst,", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 353.3655090332031, 456.3771667480469, 369.4237365722656]}, {"text": "- Phospholipid PL3 is a charged molecule at physiological pH values, and it exists as pair of enantiomers.", "bbox": [56.6929931640625, 371.29852294921875, 538.578369140625, 384.8657531738281]}, {"text": "5.6", "bbox": [78.60798645019531, 394.2635192871094, 92.84232330322266, 407.83074951171875]}, {"text": "Draw the structures of PL2 and PL3 using R to show the fatty acid residues.", "bbox": [114.6925277709961, 394.26348876953125, 480.581298828125, 407.83074951171875]}, {"text": "Show stereochemistry where appropriate.", "bbox": [114.69099426269531, 406.2184753417969, 312.1720275878906, 419.7857360839844]}, {"text": "3.0 pt", "bbox": [495.4499816894531, 394.1885070800781, 521.8193969726562, 407.7557373046875]}]}]